type: article
title: "THOX MeshStack: Capacity-Priced Pipeline Sharding, Grant-Gated KV Transfer and Lease-Fenced Device Roles for a Private Household Mesh"
authors:
  - family-names: Ross
    given-names: Craig
    affiliation: "THOX.ai LLC"
  - family-names: Xaypanya
    given-names: Tommy
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4425-9565"
    affiliation: "THOX.ai LLC"
institution:
  name: "THOX.ai Research, THOX.ai LLC"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/Thox-ai/thox-whitepapers/resolve/main/meshstack/THOX_MeshStack_Research_Paper_v1.0.1.pdf"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  MeshStack is the distributed-inference layer for the THOX device
  family: a private household mesh of small computers that pool memory
  and compute for local-first AI. This report reconciles two design
  lineages (storage-aware parallelism; pipeline sharding with a KV
  graph and a secrets grant graph) and the Auto Device Role Mode lease
  design into one priced, grant-gated, lease-fenced system. Pipeline
  stage placement is priced against each node's storage and RAM floors;
  KV cache moves between nodes only under an explicit grant; device
  roles are held under epoch-bearing leases so a departed holder cannot
  act on a stale authorisation. Evidence is classed measured (general
  host), calculated (public device floors), or simulated (protocol
  logic); no engine throughput, cross-host transfer, or physical-device
  measurement is claimed. Headline results: lossless KV compression
  1.512x on the byte-split proxy at 121.9 MB/s encode; HMAC chunk keying
  9.67 microseconds per 64-token chunk; at public floors an Air+Mini+Clip
  trio cannot place the 27.8B reference model (12 GB trio floor vs
  14.6 GiB Q4 weights) and is returned Unplaceable; under churn
  simulation, epoch fencing rejects all stale completions and live
  grant evaluation authorises zero accesses after a grant-path node
  departs.
keywords:
  - MeshStack
  - ThoxOS
  - pipeline parallelism
  - KV cache
  - distributed inference
  - local-first AI
  - HMAC
  - leases
  - LoRa
